Subject: [PATCH 11/11] feat(pqc-m11): APNs ML-DSA-65 dual signature envelope
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PQC migration (whitepaper 1.3): Apple APNs JWT (ES256) is unchanged
because the Apple protocol is not ours to evolve. M11 adds an
app-layer dual-signature envelope that legacy clients verify with
Ed25519 and post-quantum clients verify with ML-DSA-65. Both halves
must verify; failure of either throws.

- src/security/push-dual-signature.ts:
  - signPushPayloadDual takes a UTF-8 payload, a 32-byte raw Ed25519
    secret, a 4032-byte raw ML-DSA-65 secret, and per-algorithm keyIds.
    It builds PKCS8 / SPKI framing on top of node:crypto for the
    Ed25519 half (NEVER @noble/curves/ed25519 — that path is missing
    randomPrivateKey and breaks vitest, per danteng prompt §M11.2) and
    reuses the canonical ML-DSA-65 helpers from M1.
  - verifyPushPayloadDual fails closed: it deserialises the envelope,
    checks the strict `algorithms: ["ed25519", "ml-dsa-65"]` header
    (length 2, exact ordering — no reordering, no extras), verifies
    the Ed25519 half, then the ML-DSA-65 half, and only returns true
    when both pass.
  - Envelope wire format: algorithms, ed25519_sig, mldsa65_sig,
    key_id_ed25519, key_id_mldsa65 — base64url-encoded signatures,
    JSON-serializable.
  - All input shapes (raw key length, keyId presence, signature
    length) are validated up front; PushDualSignatureError is the
    typed error class.
- src/security/push-dual-signature.test.ts: 13 invariants — sign +
  verify round-trip, fail-closed on tampered Ed25519 sig, fail-closed
  on tampered ML-DSA-65 sig, fail-closed on tampered payload, key
  mismatch (Ed25519 and ML-DSA-65), strict algorithms header
  (reordering + extras), JSON-stringified envelope round-trip,
  non-object envelope rejection, raw-key length guards, empty /
  over-long keyId rejection, and exact signature byte counts (64
  Ed25519, 3309 ML-DSA-65).

13/13 green.

